WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.421
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:07.852
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:14.880
Unit sixteen: Sport and Competition. In this unit, you will talk about sport, competitions and past events.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:16.757
athlete.

5
00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:19.944
athlete means a person who is very good at sport.

6
00:00:20.244 --> 00:00:23.103
Cambodian athletes won medals at the SEA Games.

7
00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:25.677
Your turn. Say: athlete.

8
00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:29.239
athlete.

9
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.205
qualify.

10
00:00:31.905 --> 00:00:35.146
qualify means to win a place in the next stage of a competition.

11
00:00:35.446 --> 00:00:37.342
Our team qualified for the final.

12
00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:40.020
Your turn. Say: qualify.

13
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.733
qualify.

14
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:45.532
defeat.

15
00:00:46.232 --> 00:00:49.497
defeat means a loss in a competition; to beat someone.

16
00:00:49.797 --> 00:00:51.808
It was their first defeat of the season.

17
00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:54.568
Your turn. Say: defeat.

18
00:00:57.268 --> 00:00:58.107
defeat.

19
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:00.199
opponent team.

20
00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:03.258
opponent team means the team you play against.

21
00:01:03.558 --> 00:01:06.173
The opponent team was faster but less organised.

22
00:01:06.873 --> 00:01:09.723
Your turn. Say: opponent team.

23
00:01:12.423 --> 00:01:13.563
opponent team.

24
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.737
personal best.

25
00:01:16.437 --> 00:01:19.772
personal best means the best result a person has ever achieved.

26
00:01:20.072 --> 00:01:23.406
She ran her personal best in the 100 metres.

27
00:01:24.106 --> 00:01:26.515
Your turn. Say: personal best.

28
00:01:29.215 --> 00:01:30.425
personal best.

29
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:32.580
record holder.

30
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.789
record holder means the person with the best result ever in an event.

31
00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:39.321
He is the national record holder in swimming.

32
00:01:40.021 --> 00:01:42.696
Your turn. Say: record holder.

33
00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:46.583
record holder.

34
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:48.701
sportsmanship.

35
00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:52.608
sportsmanship means fair and polite behaviour in sport.

36
00:01:52.908 --> 00:01:55.940
Shaking hands after a match shows good sportsmanship.

37
00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.362
Your turn. Say: sportsmanship.

38
00:02:02.062 --> 00:02:03.238
sportsmanship.

39
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.112
training camp.

40
00:02:05.812 --> 00:02:09.808
training camp means a place where athletes train together for a period.

41
00:02:10.108 --> 00:02:12.653
The team spent a month at a training camp in Thailand.

42
00:02:13.353 --> 00:02:16.284
Your turn. Say: training camp.

43
00:02:18.984 --> 00:02:19.997
training camp.

44
00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:22.925
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:23.225 --> 00:02:25.619
Did you watch the football final last night?

46
00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:31.055
Yes! I couldn't believe they had qualified after losing the first match.

47
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:35.023
They had trained at a training camp for two months.

48
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:40.467
That explains it. Before the game, they had never beaten that opponent team.

49
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:44.990
And the captain showed great sportsmanship after the whistle.

50
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:49.258
He had scored his personal best: three goals!

51
00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.584
Grammar focus: Past perfect.

52
00:02:52.884 --> 00:02:56.753
Use the past perfect for an action that happened before another past action.

53
00:02:57.053 --> 00:02:58.960
Had plus past participle.

54
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.782
For example: She won because she had trained hard.

55
00:03:02.082 --> 00:03:05.881
We often use already, never, just and by the time with the past perfect.

56
00:03:06.883 --> 00:03:09.524
Now read and listen. A Champion's Comeback.

57
00:03:09.824 --> 00:03:14.796
Before the 2023 SEA Games, the young runner had suffered a serious injury.

58
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:18.675
Many people believed that she had finished her career.

59
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:23.214
However, she had spent six months at a training camp to recover.

60
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:28.594
In the final, she defeated the record holder and ran her personal best.

61
00:03:29.883 --> 00:03:33.137
She later said that she had learned more from defeat than from victory.

62
00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.835
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:37.135 --> 00:03:39.820
A person who is very good at sport is an blank.

64
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.901
A, athlete. B, opponent team. C, training camp.

65
00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:49.580
The answer is A: athlete.

66
00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:52.781
When we arrived, the game blank.

67
00:03:53.081 --> 00:03:57.489
A, already started. B, had already started. C, has already started.

68
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:03.657
The answer is B: had already started.

69
00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.184
He was tired because he blank all day.

70
00:04:07.484 --> 00:04:10.720
A, had worked. B, works. C, has worked.

71
00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:16.391
The answer is A: had worked.

72
00:04:17.883 --> 00:04:20.208
Fair and polite behaviour in sport is blank.

73
00:04:20.508 --> 00:04:24.324
A, defeat. B, sportsmanship. C, personal best.

74
00:04:28.317 --> 00:04:30.339
The answer is B: sportsmanship.

75
00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.674
According to the text, before the games the runner blank.

76
00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:38.976
A, had won a medal. B, had suffered an injury. C, had retired.

77
00:04:42.983 --> 00:04:45.552
The answer is B: had suffered an injury.

78
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:51.386
Now it's your turn to speak. Tell me about a time you or your team won or lost something.

79
00:04:56.686 --> 00:05:01.216
Our team lost the final because we had not practised enough, but we learned a lot.

80
00:05:01.516 --> 00:05:03.051
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.411
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past perfect.

82
00:05:07.711 --> 00:05:11.547
Today's value is fair play. Play fairly and follow the rules.

83
00:05:11.847 --> 00:05:14.581
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.754
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

